    83	
    84	A partition $\C'$ of a set $\PP$ is a \emph{proper refinement} of a partition $\C$ of $\PP$ if each part in $\C'$ is a subset of some part in $\C$, and at least one of these inclusions is proper. We write $\C' \prec \C$ if $\C'$ is a proper refinement of $\C$. In the designs that we consider, a point-transitive subgroup of automorphisms leaves invariant a chain of partitions ordered by $\prec$. We introduce the following concepts.
    85	
    86	\begin{definition} \label{def:chain} 
    87	Let $s\geq 2$, let $\PP$ be a set,  and let $G\leq \Sym(\PP)$. 
    88	We say that the action of $G$ on $\PP$ is \emph{$s$-chain-imprimitive} if $G$ is transitive and
    89	there exist $G$-invariant partitions $\C_0, \C_1, \ldots, \C_s$ of $\PP$, which form a chain
    90	    \begin{equation} \label{eq:chain}
    91	    \Ch : \ {\textstyle\binom{\PP}{1}} = \C_0 \prec \C_1 \prec \cdots \prec \C_{s-1} \prec \C_s = \{\PP\}. 
    92	    \end{equation}
    93	under the partial order $\prec$. If $\D$ is a design with point set $\PP$, such that $G \leq \Aut(\D)$ acts $s$-chain-imprimitively on  $\PP$, then we say that $\D$ is \emph{$(G,s)$-chain-imprimitive}.
    94	\end{definition}
