   605	Since $v = e_1e_2e_3 = p^8 + p^4 + 1$ and $k = p^4 + 1$, we again have $k(k-1) = v-1$ so that $\lambda = \frac{b}{v}$ where $b := |\B|$. By Lemma \ref{lem:array-equiv}(b) the block set $\B = B_3^G$ consists of all $k$-element subsets $B$ of $\PP$ whose array function $\chi_{B}$ is $G$-equivalent to $\chi_{B_3}$. In order to find $b$, observe that the intersection of the generating block $B_3$ in \eqref{B:s=3} and the $\C_2$-class $C_{(0)}$ (the first column in Figure \ref{fig:s=3}) is the set $B_2 \times \{0\}$, where $B_2$ is the generating block of the design in Example \ref{con:s=2} given in \eqref{B:s=2}. For any subset $B'_2 \in B_2^{S_{e_1} \wr S_{e_2}}$, the set $(B'_2 \times \{0\}) \cup \big\{ (0,0,\delta_3) \ | \ \delta_3 \in \mathbb{Z}^*_{e_3} \big\}$ is also a block in $\B$. Let $b_2 := \big|B_2^{S_{e_1} \wr S_{e_2}}\big|$; then
   606	    \[
   607	    b
   608	    = b_2 \cdot |\C_2| \cdot (\#\text{points in a $\C_2$-class})^{e_3-1}
   609	    = b_2 \cdot e_3 \cdot c_2^{e_3-1}.
   610	    \]
   611	We found in Example \ref{con:s=2} that $b_2 = \binom{e_1-1}{p} \cdot \frac{e_1e_2}{p+1} \cdot c_1^{e_2-1}$; substituting this into the above gives
   612	    \[
   613	    b = \binom{e_1-1}{p} \cdot \frac{v}{p+1} \cdot c_1^{e_2-1} \cdot c_2^{e_3-1}
   614	    \]
   615	and therefore $\lambda = \binom{e_1-1}{p} \cdot \frac{1}{p+1} \cdot c_1^{e_2-1} \cdot c_2^{e_3-1}$.
   616	\end{construction}
